WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.020
For my father intelligence was all that
matters.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.040
Ever since my brother Charles was
diagnosed to be a gifted child all he

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.900
talked about were IQ and intelligence
research. W high IQ apparently strongly

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.520
predicts good grades, a good career, and
even health and mortality and stuff. His

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.500
favorite story is Kim Ung-Yong a Korean
with an official IQ of 210. Just six

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.460
months old he was already speaking
fluent Korean and at age 3 wrote essays

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.449
in German and English. Then he would hug
Charles and look at me with this

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:35.859
question in his face. I hated that I
wondered if I could reach my little

00:00:35.859 --> 00:00:40.449
brother in anything? When I was young me
and my dad were best buddies.

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:45.339
He never even cared much about IQ or G
or whatever. When my brother started

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:50.109
reading at just 2 years old everything
changed. Suddenly I was forgotten and

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:56.170
soon after I was the slow one. Once when
I got a C in math he didn't even look at

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:01.329
my paper and just told Charles that an
ape is believed to have an IQ of 40. I

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:07.930
hated his sarcasm. Once at dinner when he
started talking about intelligence or "G"

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.979
he'd say - G stands for general
intelligence and scientists say it

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:16.689
exists because apparently most IQ tests
correlate - whatever - he was talking

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:21.430
about it and then drew up this graph on
a piece of paper saying: "look boy this is

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.289
the distribution of intelligence of all
people in town 0.1% of people will have

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:34.020
an IQ of 55 or below, 2% have an IQ
between 55 to 70, 14% between 70 and 85,

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.369
34% will score between 85 and the
average which is set at a hundred.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:46.929
Thirty-four have an IQ between 100 and
115 and 14% between 115 to 132.

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:53.829
2% have an IQ higher than 130 and only 0.1%
will have an IQ of a genius of 145 or

00:01:53.829 --> 00:01:58.479
above, like your little brother." I told
him I'm not interested. I guess I

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:04.060
shouldn't have. He exploded "Not
interested? Do you know what this all means

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.710
boy?" He turned the paper around and
started all over:  "It means that if you

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.480
take 1,000 people then one has some
form of mental

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.760
retardation, which means trouble living
alone. 20 will have difficulty reading

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.650
the map. 140 can perform simple tasks at
work but cannot qualify to become a

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:28.590
soldier in the US Army. 340 probably
finished high school and another 340

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:34.590
will go to college. Maybe 140 can do a
Ph.D. and later work as surgeons. 20 are

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:39.269
capable of producing a significant
scientific work and only one will make

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:45.900
it into an Ivy League college like MIT
where the average IQ is 145. Your little

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:51.390
brother got an IQ higher than that!"
A few weeks later was career day at my

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:55.079
school. Some people in suits showed up
and told us about a new form of

00:02:55.079 --> 00:02:58.530
cognitive assessment we could be doing
which would help us find the right job.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.599
The technical term is the Wechsler IQ
score. When I heard the words IQ I got

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.370
completely sweaty hands my heart started
racing. This could be the moment of truth.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.810
Then one woman started speaking. She told
us that we are now going to take a test

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.430
and just 1 week later we all get the
results with some specific ideas about

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.930
our future career path. She said it takes
only 90 minutes and measures our

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.190
intelligence in the following four areas:
perceptual reasoning, verbal

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:31.590
comprehension, working memory and
processing speed. The assessment was

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.790
voluntary and my friend instantly stood
up to leave the class, showing what he

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.329
thought about this whole thing. My
heart still racing I wasn't sure what

00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:43.230
to do and kept seated. Our teacher then
handed out some questions, when she

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:47.069
passed by my table she simply said:
"you gonna do fine here". I don't think

00:03:47.069 --> 00:03:51.480
she realized this but I was so happy to
hear her say that! Maybe I'm not all that

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.889
bad at these stupid IQ tests? Maybe it's
a day that I can actually show my dad

00:03:55.889 --> 00:04:01.799
who I really am? What shall I do? I was so
ready to show my dad that I'm no idiot, I

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:06.670
decided to stay.
I turned the first page over it read the

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.349
following: perceptual reasoning is the
ability to think and reason with visual

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:15.909
information. It is the ability to see
what is being asked and to organize

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:20.620
information in our heads through images.
The first question was: When folded into

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:28.090
a cube, which of the following corners
would touch corner A?  D, B, E or C? I tried

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.030
to fold the cube in my head and - yeah it
worked!

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:37.090
It must be "D". The second section was
about working memory: our ability to keep

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:41.800
several chunks of information in our
mind simultaneously. One of the questions

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:47.919
was: what is the next number in the
series: 4, 12, 6, 9, 8, 6 ?

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:51.591
There were four options: 6, 5, 10 or 12

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:54.699
The trick here was to put all the

00:04:54.699 --> 00:05:02.380
digits in my head and look for a pattern:
4 X 6 X 8 X which means the next would

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:08.169
be 10! The third section was verbal
comprehension, which measures our ability

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:12.639
to access vocabulary, express ourselves
in a meaningful manner and apply

00:05:12.639 --> 00:05:16.240
reasoning skills to information
presented verbally. In the first

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:21.010
question it said: what is the difference
between the words "refuted" an "irrefutable"?

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:26.139
Do they have similar meanings, have
contradicting meanings or mean neither

00:05:26.139 --> 00:05:32.110
the same nor the opposite? They must have
contradicting meanings! The fourth

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:36.130
section was about processing speed: the
pace at which we take in new information

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:41.380
and make sense of it in order to prepare
a response. One of the questions asked

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:48.250
was: what is the 12th letter of the
alphabet is it: T, L, R or B? I realized

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.680
I had to rule out all the options that
didn't look right,

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:56.199
counting would have taken way too long, L
is the right answer! I had completed all

00:05:56.199 --> 00:06:01.240
of the 50 questions in time and I was
very relieved. In the end, the woman said:

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.979
"A lot of research over the last century
went into the IQ test we had just taken

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:10.330
and there is convincing evidence that
our intelligence is mainly a product of

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:13.700
our genes. There is an estimate of a
heritability range from

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:18.140
50% to 90% although the environment also
matters,"

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:22.730
she continued: "especially negative
influences during your childhood like

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:27.920
infectious disease, malnutrition, air
pollution, or led in the paint of your

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.170
walls at home. These things can reduce
your IQ forever." She explained that it's

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:37.580
because during the prenatal period and
early years of life a child's brain

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.320
consumes a huge part of the body's
energy to grow, and if the body was under

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.280
attack it cannot support the brain's
growth to its full potential. In other

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:50.960
words you were born with a pretty fixed
IQ. Good parents and schools can keep the

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:56.060
IQ at its genetically predefined level
and maybe increase it a bit, negative

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:01.790
influences, however, can surely reduce it
a lot. "I am just saying this" she closed

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:05.780
"because if you are getting your results
next week and you are not happy with

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:10.040
your score or our recommendation, then
know, that there is little you can do

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:15.230
about that. Even if you practice for
years or continue school indefinitely,

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:20.150
it's almost impossible to improve your
score by more than 10 points. Just think

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:25.520
about that before you open that envelope.
You don't have to."  When the envelope was

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.050
handed to me a week later I got excited
to open it. I took a deep breath, but

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:35.450
before I ripped the cover apart I halted-
do I really want this? Why do I care so

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:40.580
much? Do I really want to compete with my
brother? And if so what does this prove?

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:44.810
There are so many aspects of my life
that matter more than my measured

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:50.300
intelligence. I'm probably no genius but
I know I did well. But more importantly I

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:56.000
know that I don't need to prove anything
to anyone! I decided not to open the

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:01.460
envelope and I loved this new idea of
myself - free from these limitations!

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.830
I felt like I had grown up.  Now when I
heard my father speak all proud about

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:12.080
Charles, I just smiled. I realized that
it's not that he loved him more, no my

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.790
brother just gave my dad the chance to
get attention, to be someone. He's the dad

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:21.910
of a genius and not just another middle
manager at the bank on middle street.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:26.170
A few years later I dropped out of
college and started my own company and

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:30.610
soon after fell in love with a wonderful
woman and also started a family. My

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.150
brother is now a professor at a famous
university, but never found the right

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.020
girl and like many very smart people
suffers from depressions.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:42.370
My dad doesn't care so much about IQ
anymore, he's now a proud grandfather.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:46.720
They say it takes intelligence to know
how to do things right but wisdom to do

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:52.860
the right thing. Leaving that envelope
closed was the best decision of my life!

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:58.150
Here are five questions from a real IQ
test, you've got five seconds each. When

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:01.120
you are done post your answers in the
comments: Good luck!

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:06.400
1. A package of gift cards has a length
of eight centimeters a width of four

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.930
centimeters and a volume of 64
centimeters cubed. What is the height of

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:11.430
the box?

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:21.700
2. Some Bargles are Chongos
and some Chongos are Munhattsens. Are

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:29.495
some Bargles definitely Munhattsens?
Yes or No?

00:09:29.495 --> 00:09:33.310
3. Max needed to get seven

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:37.600
new doors from the home improvement
store for his house. His car could only

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.530
hold two doors at once.
How many times did max have to visit the

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:47.430
store? 2, 4, 7, 8 or 9?

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:55.370
4. Art is to wall as cup is to: handle,
coffee, cupboard, rim, nail?

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:19.320
5. what is the missing number in the series: 1, 16, 81
blank 625, 1296?

